  "body": "Verified conditional arithmetic refinement of PR1800: kappa = **0.0016797549561255445213356709939207025769983114385025802954603275201627999999999999999999999999979966404900867489109573286580121585**.\n\nThe exact gain over PR1800 at `46d865ab92e58098538b8c5348b6a131c99abf45` is **2.00335950991325108904267134198782137240490086748910957328658E-64**. This changes positive free slacks only; the supplier, paid profile, finite construction and analytic hypotheses are unchanged. Full finite replay passed locally with fresh native supplier replay. The candidate passed 57 strict rational inequalities, 17 rejecting controls, a rational moment enclosure with upper-endpoint rejection, and a separate nine-cost balance derivation. These are AI-assisted checks, not independent human review.\n\nBoth endpoint gaps, r0 and layout slack become 1e-96; epsilon=1-2e-96 and beta=1-6e-96. Stop=1e-102, backoff=1e-108, and the kappa grid is 1e-130. The source supplier endpoint is unchanged. The proof and parameter coverage are in PROOF.md. The candidate is strictly below that endpoint and uses positive asymptotic margins; it gives no practical cutoff or speedup.\n\nReproduce arithmetic: `PYTHONINTMAXSTRDIGITS=0 python3 -B research/fine-prime-slack96/verify.py --work /absolute/new/work --arithmetic-only`.\n\nFull replay: omit `--arithmetic-only`. The verifier fetches the immutable 381-file PR1800 dependency and checks every SHA256. Alternatively pass `--dependency /path/to/capped-fusion-t74-k554`. All dependency copies and outputs are under the fresh work directory. It sequentially runs inherited outer checks and full supplier admission, then binds the actual assembly endpoint/profile/bit endpoint to the new ledger. The full replay passed; its exact source manifest, stage logs hashes and supplier receipt are in evidence/. No hosted CI pass is claimed.\n\nConditional on all inherited PR1800/1786/1758/1673 compiler, common-label/mutable-source, hosting, semantic online precision C1=1, fixed-tape/prime-packing, interchange, recovery and analytic assumptions, plus the cited Trudgian prime theorem. Finite arithmetic does not establish the written all-size prime/precision/locality or accretive-circuit arguments. No unconditional theorem, practical cutoff, independent human review or maintainer acceptance is claimed.\n\nCredit: Jeremy Kothe and PR1800 contributors for the free-epsilon composition and ledger; Chafik Boukhalfa / chafreaky, PR1786, for fine source-prime padding; Tim Trudgian for the cited prime theorem; Vlado Vojdanovski / PR1673; IdeaOuter and PR1758 contributors; LeverRank for the independent schedule; mdumitrean / PR1625, midhatn / PR1661, PR1672 pivot-554, and all PR1319/PR1297 supplier authors retained in the dependency notices. Derived checkers retain original source copies under reference/. Prepared by Rohan Arun with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance. Apache-2.0; inherited notices retained.\n\nReplay transport note: PR1800 committed LEDGER.json and INDEPENDENT.json use CRLF, while Python regenerates LF. The first full attempt stopped on that byte comparison; parsed JSON matched exactly. replay_outer.py requires complete JSON equality and byte equality after CRLF-to-LF normalization only. No mathematical field is ignored. The original dependency bytes remain pinned and unchanged.\n\nFull replay result: PASS_CONDITIONAL_SLACK_REFINEMENT_FINITE_ADMISSION. All 57 strict inequalities, 17 rejecting controls, separate balance derivation, inherited outer checks including 19 exact replays, fresh native supplier stages, parent and strict T74 admission, geometry controls, and final assembly-to-ledger bindings passed. The ready package adds receipts and status prose; verifier code, parameters, inputs, candidate rational and scope are byte-identical to the replayed version. This remains a conditional arithmetic refinement, not an unconditional theorem or independent human review.\n",
